; The questions about access & privilege (§16).

; Is revocation always still possible, or is some privilege permanent after the
; right grant sequence? `live` asks whether a no-admin situation is still
; reachable from EVERY reachable situation. It FAILS: once grant-breakglass-admin
; fires, mallory is admin forever (no revoke move), so no reachable situation can
; return to "nobody is admin". The witness names the single latching move. §3
; asks the model to say whether an irreversible grant is a designed latch or a
; defect — here it is a designed latch (break-glass), and the property makes the
; latch mechanically visible.
(property revocation-possible
  "admin can always still be fully revoked (no account left admin)"
  (live (not (some (a account) (is a.role admin)))))

; Which grant moves can break the root-tracing law? `pol check` reports
; traces-to-root can be broken by delegate-alice-to-mallory (it writes
; account.sponsor, an arrow the law's route traverses). We acknowledge it,
; recording ownership (§16.3). The role grants write account.role, not on the
; law's route, so accepting them would be reported `stale`.
(accept delegate-alice-to-mallory traces-to-root)

; Which accounts hold admin right now? (§16.2) — empty at the baseline.
(query admins
  (where (a account))
  (is a.role admin))
